{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-280671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,1,2⟩$, $y=⟨-3,2,0⟩$, and $z=⟨4,-2,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))-1((-3)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 4)+2((-3)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2+3-4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|1|=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-280671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $y=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, and $z=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1-4-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,5,0⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0)+3(-20) \\\\  & =30-0-60 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-30|=30.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-280712" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280712" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-128433" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128433" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "38"] ["math" "66"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128433" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "26"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $x=⟨3,1,4⟩$, $y=⟨0,2,5⟩$, and $z=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 0)-(0\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 6)+4(0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =6+30-48 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-12|=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-280716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280716" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨8,0,3⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,1⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)-(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3)+4(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-3k+1+32 \\\\  & =33-3k \\\\  & =3(11-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 3(11-k) & =0 \\\\ 11-k & =0 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{14}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨0,3,6⟩$, $q=⟨t,t,2⟩$, and $r=⟨-1,2,7⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ t & t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}|+6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & t \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(t\\cdot 7-(-1)\\cdot 2)+6(t\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot t) \\\\  & =-21t-6+12t+6t \\\\  & =-3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -3t-6 & =0 \\\\ -3t & =6 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-73735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $t$ given that the vectors $a=⟨3,-1,7⟩,$ $b=⟨t,4,t⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,6,8⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 7 \\\\ t & 4 & t \\\\ 2 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & t \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & t \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(4\\cdot 8-6\\cdot t)+(t\\cdot 8-2\\cdot t)+7(t\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =96-18t+8t-2t+42t-56 \\\\  & =30t+40 \\\\  & =10(3t+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 10(3t+4) & =0 \\\\ 3t+4 & =0 \\\\ t & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-\\frac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-128456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,t,1⟩,$ $q=⟨3,2,6⟩,$ and $r=⟨3,4,0⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}t & t & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t(2\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 6)-t(3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 6)+(3\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-24t+18t+6 \\\\  & =-6t+6 \\\\  & =6(1-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 6(1-t) & =0 \\\\ 1-t & =0 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-128454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,k,k⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,2⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 0)-k(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 4)+k(0\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =15+8k-12k \\\\  & =15-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 15-4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =15 \\\\ k & =\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{15}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-280729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-280729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{15}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,1,3),$ $B(0,5,5),$ $C(3,4,5),$ and $D(2,0,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =4j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+2k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+2k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =2i-1j-1k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4(3\\cdot -1-2\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-281029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(5,1,4),$ $B(4,1,7),$ $C(3,1,5),$ and $D(2,3,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+7k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+j+5k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+k \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+3k)-(5i+j+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1)-0+3((-2)\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2-12 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-10|=10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-128483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-8+1)+3(-4-1)+3(1-(-2)) \\\\  & =-21-15+9 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-27|=27.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(7,6,4),$ $B(8,5,9),$ $C(7,4,2),$ and $D(5,7,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(8i+5j+9k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =i-j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(7i+4j+2k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+7j+4k)-(7i+6j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+j \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-2))+(0\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+5(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2-4-20 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-22|=22.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-128475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-128475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,-1,2)$, $B(-2,2,3)$, $C(1,1,1)$, and $D(-1,3,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+2j+3k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j-2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot (-4)-4\\cdot (-1))-3(0\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot (-1))+(0\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12+6+4 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|22|=22.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378"} {"question" "q-73745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "22"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "q-73745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2342aa3991117eddf4770ed83b6fa4ca1f0d083b9d86d8bcc9f885c7b00f83b"} {"question" "e-4350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4350.json" "file_sha256" "586799041ff3e08eb8ad0af1ea5303ee47b721102cfdddf503e7f78f3946a0d3"} {"question" "e-4350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4350.json" "file_sha256" "586799041ff3e08eb8ad0af1ea5303ee47b721102cfdddf503e7f78f3946a0d3"} {"question" "e-4351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4351.json" "file_sha256" "aaf511d232f4dcc97de3dab904c9507b208301e2678ae5c00c325b4f58a7a7b7"} {"question" "e-4351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4351.json" "file_sha256" "aaf511d232f4dcc97de3dab904c9507b208301e2678ae5c00c325b4f58a7a7b7"} {"question" "e-4352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4352.json" "file_sha256" "fb48d45a8e3b284975c75b39d6c82156810e55342147290d26b931e3ee83bd05"} {"question" "e-4352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4352.json" "file_sha256" "fb48d45a8e3b284975c75b39d6c82156810e55342147290d26b931e3ee83bd05"}] "usage" {"e-4351" [] "e-4350" [] "e-4352" []} "basis" 1397 "retractions" [[17592186105519 :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle$."] [17592186105519 :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}1 & - 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & - 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = 1 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert - ( - 4 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert + 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & - 2 \\\\ - 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = ( - 2 \\cdot  3 - 1 \\cdot  0 ) + 4 ( 0 \\cdot  3 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) + 2 ( 0 \\cdot  0 - ( - 1 ) \\cdot  ( - 2 ) ) \\\\  & = - 6 + 4 - 4 \\\\  & = - 6\\end{array}$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = \\mid -6 \\mid = 6\n$$"] [17592186105520 :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar."] [17592186105520 :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ - 2 & - 1 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = k \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert - 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert + 1 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & - 1 \\\\ - 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = k ( - 1 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  1 ) - 2 ( - 2 \\cdot  2 - ( - 1 ) \\cdot  1 ) + ( - 2 \\cdot  1 - ( - 1 ) \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) \\\\  & = - 3 k + 6 - 3 \\\\  & = - 3 k + 3.\\end{array}$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = 0 \\\\ - 3 k + 3 & = 0 \\\\ k & = 1\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."] [17592186105521 :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-1,2)$, $B(2,1,1)$, $C(-1,2,1)$, and $D(4,4,2)$."] [17592186105521 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} & = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( 2 \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} ) - ( 3 \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = - \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 1 , 2 , - 1 \\rangle \\\\ \\overrightarrow{AC} & = \\mathbf{c} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( - \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} ) - ( 3 \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = - 4 \\mathbf{i} + 3 \\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 4 , 3 , - 1 \\rangle \\\\ \\overrightarrow{AD} & = \\mathbf{d} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( 4 \\mathbf{i} + 4 \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) - ( 3 \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = \\mathbf{i} + 5 \\mathbf{j} \\\\  & = \\langle  1 , 5 , 0 \\rangle\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} \\cdot  ( \\overrightarrow{AC} \\times  \\overrightarrow{AD} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}- 1 & 2 & - 1 \\\\ - 4 & 3 & - 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = ( - 1 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert - 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 4 & - 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = - ( 3 \\cdot  0 - 5 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) - 2 ( ( - 4 ) \\cdot  0 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) - ( ( - 4 ) \\cdot  5 - 1 \\cdot  3 ) \\\\  & = - 5 - 2 + 23 \\\\  & = 16.\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV= \\mid 16 &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
